WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:04.530
Let us talk through another example.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:10.047
When you try to socialize with people who
you do not know, your tinnitus interferes

00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:14.810
so much that you only understand about
50% of what is being communicated.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.470
Let us think about the stressful
aspects of this situation.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.610
The first unchangeable aspect
is that you have tinnitus.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.484
Second, tinnitus is interfering
with your ability to communicate,

00:00:28.524 --> 00:00:33.270
which is no doubt frustrating
and or embarrassing for you.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.529
One thing you can do
is to educate the person a little

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:40.270
about why you are having so
much trouble communicating.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.691
What is unchangeable about the situation
is that you do not have control

00:00:44.731 --> 00:00:48.130
over how the stranger reacts when
you tell them about your tinnitus.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.170
They may react with sympathy.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:55.085
If they do not react the way you
want them to, then you can use some

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:59.890
of the stress management strategies
that will be introduced in upcoming sections.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.778
Please note that our focus
in this coping with tinnitus

00:01:04.818 --> 00:01:09.430
course is on stress management
rather than stress mastery.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.990
There are some situations
we cannot master.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.286
For example, the cause
of some of your stress,

00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:19.525
such as tinnitus, cannot totally
be eliminated from your life,

00:01:19.565 --> 00:01:24.670
but it can be managed, and its
impact on you can be modified.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.905
Remember that the first
question about a stress

00:01:27.945 --> 00:01:30.990
you can ask yourself
is, is this changeable?

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:34.264
We all have things in our lives
that frustrate or annoy us,

00:01:34.304 --> 00:01:36.350
but that we cannot change, like tinnitus.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.810
But there are specific aspects
of tinnitus that you can change.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.791
This coping with tinnitus
course encourages you

00:01:43.831 --> 00:01:47.550
to take action when you
can change a situation.

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.704
When you cannot act to change
the source of stress,

00:01:50.744 --> 00:01:54.886
then we encourage you to acknowledge
your feelings and engage in specific

00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:59.370
stress reduction strategies that can
help you optimally manage your feelings.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:03.090
These strategies will be
taught in other sections.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:08.772
Feelings are not necessarily wrong
or bad or something to avoid or suppress,

00:02:08.812 --> 00:02:11.690
but your feelings may cause you distress.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:16.870
Having tinnitus may cause you to be
frustrated or angry or enraged.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.980
That is understandable
because it is a condition

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:23.490
that you probably do not
like or want to have.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.071
This course will coach you in strategies
so that you can tackle these

00:02:28.111 --> 00:02:33.450
stress reactions and be more in control
over how you react to events.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.441
Asking yourself whether you can
change the issues causing you stress

00:02:39.481 --> 00:02:43.290
will help you think about your choice
of response to the stress.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.150
Your ability to choose
coping strategies will

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.890
give you more flexibility,
options, and control.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.490
This approach acknowledges
that you have choices.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:03:00.333
Sometimes you should try to change things
to get rid of a stress, such as a new job,

00:03:00.373 --> 00:03:05.690
avoid a specific situation, obtain
hearing aids with tinnitus filters.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.381
Other times you are dealing with a stressful
situation that is unchangeable.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.180
Trying to change the unchangeable
may cause you more

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:17.110
stress and possibly make
your tinnitus symptoms increase.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:21.077
By making coping choices that are more
appropriate to the type of stress,

00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:26.170
you will be coping more effectively
and experiencing more control in your life.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.130
You are in the driver's seat.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:36.190
Let us end this section by going through
a short stress management exercise.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:40.006
This is a brief relaxation
practice that you can

00:03:40.046 --> 00:03:44.510
use to alter your reaction
to unchangeable stress.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:50.490
Note that you may want to play soothing
music when you practice this technique.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.343
Otherwise, for some people,

00:03:52.383 --> 00:03:57.490
tinnitus may become more noticeable
in quiet exercises like these.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:03.270
First, find a relaxing
position in your chair.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:09.290
Sit in your chair with your feet
flat on the floor or propped up.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:18.630
Place your hands in your lap
or on the arms of the chair.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:25.130
Make sure you are comfortable.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:32.420
Now take several deep, slow breaths.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.660
Try to breathe deeply from your diaphragm.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:49.400
Select a peaceful image, such as a forest,
a mountain top, or the ocean.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:01.754
Think about this peaceful place
and try to imagine more details,

00:05:01.794 --> 00:05:05.160
such as how the sun feels on your skin,

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:15.850
how it smells, what sounds you might hear.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:27.995
Imagine reaching out
and touching things around you,

00:05:28.035 --> 00:05:35.535
how the ground feels under your toes,
how a leaf feels as you hold it in your hand.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:43.340
As you imagine your tranquil
place, let yourself relax,

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.340
feel calm and peaceful.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:06.230
Take a few more deep breaths.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:10.770
Try to breathe from your diaphragm.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:22.940
Notice how your body feels
in this moment of peace.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.880
Does your body feel different?

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:36.300
When you are ready,
count back from three to one.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:43.760
Three, become aware of your surroundings.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:54.260
Two, move your feet, legs,
hands, arms and rotate your head.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:03.390
One, open your eyes, feeling relaxed.
